WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.960
Based on December's trailers alone, 2019 is
already shaping up to be a great year for

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:05.800
new movies.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:11.180
Avengers: Endgame, Captain Marvel, and Godzilla:
King of the Monsters all saw new trailers,

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.540
and that's just the beginning.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.000
"Let's do this"

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.820
Nobody would ever call 2012's Iron Sky a classic.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.090
It barely even fits the criteria for a cult
classic.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.509
And yet here we are with a sequel — and
not just any sequel, but a sequel funded with

00:00:26.509 --> 00:00:31.080
$650,000 of fans' money through an Indiegogo
campaign.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.060
Did anyone need it?

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:32.640
Nope.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.660
Did anyone want it?

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.680
Well...based on the trailer, yeah.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.660
Maybe we did want it, even if we never realized
it.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.780
The first Iron Sky, for those who never felt
like watching it, was about Nazis from the

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.040
moon who invaded Earth.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.850
Iron Sky The Coming Race pumps the gas on
the insanity, and in its own bizarre way,

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:49.600
it's beautiful.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:54.840
The trailer showcases such visual treats as
Nazis riding on dinosaurs, spaceships, people

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.550
kicking Nazis riding on dinosaurs, and lizard
Hitler.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.100
Or maybe that's dinosaur Hitler.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:00:59.700
Who can tell?

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.820
“Seig  , mother f------.”

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.680
Look for it on January 16.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.640
Aside from some leaked set photos, a trailer
released in September offered the first look

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.369
at Captain Marvel in all her superpowered,
granny-punching glory.

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:17.530
It revealed that the film would be set in
the '90s and would focus on a Carol Danvers

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:22.880
wiith amnesia who teams up with a young Nick
Fury with depth perception to fight the shapeshifting

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:23.380
Skrulls.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:27.479
The second trailer, released in December,
builds on that premise with even more Kree

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:32.679
on Skrull action and a whirlwind montage of
Danvers flying things and reading files about

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.260
her past.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.720
"I think I had a life here."

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.420
Action!

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:36.920
Intrigue!

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:37.880
Backstory!

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:41.700
Experience it all when Captain Marvel flies
into theaters on March 8.

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:47.359
It's been two years and change since Jordan
Peele's surprise smash hit Get Out hit theaters,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.409
and fans have been clamoring for a follow-up
film ever since.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.860
Well, the first trailer for Peele's sophomore
effort is here, and it's even more promising

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:55.640
than we'd hoped.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.380
The trailer for Us cranks up the terror almost
immediately, briefly introducing us to a family

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.520
on vacation before tossing them into a...well,
into a horror movie.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.119
First, their son runs off and meets a creepy
bleeding man on the beach.

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:12.030
Then, a group of masked strangers show up
at their house in the middle of the night

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.940
and reveal themselves to be the family's evil
doppelgangers.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.320
If the trailer's any indication, Us is shaping
up to be one of the scariest movies of the

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:19.820
year.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.260
Take a look on March 15.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:26.060
December gave fans the first glimpse of what's
to come for Earth's Mightiest Heroes.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.640
Well, what's left of them, anyway.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.640
As we expected, everybody's really sad in
the first trailer for Endgame.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:37.110
Half of the universe is gone, Iron Man's dying,
Captain America's crying, and Hawkeye's so

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.520
grief-stricken he's stabbing people in the
rain.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.840
The world is screwed...and yet, there's hope!

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.200
Ant-Man's back, for one.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.820
Even better, Captain Steve has a plan, which
can only mean good things.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.200
"This is gonna work Steve …”

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:49.920
“I know it is."

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.680
The game ends on April 26.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:58.080
A horror-themed spin on Superman's origin
story doesn't immediately smack of box office

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.920
success, but bear with us here.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.300
Brightburn is being executive produced by
James Gunn, who's no stranger to both indie

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.420
horror and crowd-pleasing adventures.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.460
Brightburn's trailer is fully aware of its
Smallville inspirations, which only makes

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.080
its dark turn into horror all the more satisfying.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.620
The story sees a baby crash-landing on Earth
and being adopted by a husband and wife who

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.420
live on a farm.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:24.320
As the boy grows, he begins to manifest creepy,
otherworldly powers — like Superman if he'd

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.130
been just a little more related to Satan.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:29.280
Take a look when Brightburn lands in theaters
on May 27.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.980
Amidst all the superheroes and nunnery in
today's cinematic universes, the biggest one

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.200
of them all has somehow snuck in on quiet
feet: Godzilla.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:47.120
Starting with the 2014 film, Warner Bros.
has been building a connected cinematic monster

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.680
world that's all going to come together with
Godzilla: King of the Monsters.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:55.240
The latest trailer reveals an epic film that
sees the big daddy lizard beast going head-to-head

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.940
with a bunch of kaiju while the fate of humanity
rests in the balance.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:04.510
Mothra, Rodan, and King Ghidorah all get some
facetime in the latest trailer, promising

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.940
a city-sized smackdown that will change everything.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.940
Well, at least until the next Godzilla movie.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:13.120
In the meantime, here's hoping Ghidorah gets
a shot at Godzilla's Godzisticles.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.400
Like the good old days.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:24.740
Godzilla: King of the Monsters smashes into
a theater near you on May 31.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.860
Chris Hemsworth, Liam Neeson, and Tessa Thompson
are all box office gold.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.540
They've each starred in blockbuster franchises
and proved their worth in critically acclaimed

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.720
movies, and none of them are too shabby to
look at for two hours.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:41.260
Still, we'd be remiss if we didn't mention
our reservations about Men in Black: International.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.040
The Men in Black franchise has a tendency
to be hit or miss.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:48.620
The first one was a '90s Will Smith treasure,
the second one was a shameless cash-in on

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.300
the first, and the third one breathed a little
life back into the whole shebang.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:56.180
We really want Men in Black: International
to blow us away, and we'll get the chance

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.420
to find out if it does on June 14.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.070
Check out one of our newest videos right here.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.180
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:08.300
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

